  "equipment_type": "Energy recovery ventilator (ERV) controller",
  "applies_to": "Valent energy recovery ventilators with the factory microprocessor controller, ERV program v3.10/v3.11.",
  "summary": "Valent's ERV controller offers BACnet MS/TP, BACnet IP, Modbus RTU and Modbus TCP. The BMS can enable the unit, reset alarms, write temperature, static pressure, CO2 and VOC setpoints, command supply and exhaust fan speed, enable the economizer, and send outside temperature, RH, CO2, static and VOC values from the BMS behind source-select points and a watchdog. Read-only objects cover sensors, ramps, the unit status mode, the latest alarm, fan status inputs and individual alarm flags.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP",
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": "ERV v3.10 / v3.11",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Type and access come from each section heading of the points list (e.g. 'Object Type-AV, Access-ReadCOV_Commandable'); commandable sections are shown as commandable.",
    "The list also prints a COV hysteresis and the Modbus register for each object; only the BACnet side is listed here.",
    "This ERV list is different from Valent's DOAS controller list; only about a third of the names are shared.",
    "Engineering units are not printed in the table.",
    "Source: Appendix points list, manual pages 27-32 (91 objects)."
  ],
